28-year-old chef found dead in Sanffrazisko supermarket
A 28-year-old chef, who had recently relocated to Sanfrancisko, has been found in the stairwell of a supermarket this week.
But victim's breeze says he can't imagine anyone who would hurt his brother, stating that: "His life finally began to improve."
Corpse, found near Westfield supermarket on Wednesday, has been identified as 28-year-old San Francisco resident Frank Galicia, a spokeswoman for San Francisco for Forensic Medical Exquissence Bureau said.
Sanfrancsic police announced that his death has been declared a homicide and an investigation is currently underway.
Victim's brother Luis Galicia told Sanffranzko's broadcaster ABC KGO that Frank had previously worked as a chef in Boston, but six months ago he got his dream job at Sons & Daughters San Francisco.
A spokeswoman for "Sons & Daughters" informs that the news of his death shocked them and struck them.
"We're a small team working like a cohesive family and we're going to miss him very much," a spokesman said.
In this difficult time, we are thinking with Frank's friends and family.
Luis Galicia tells that at the very beginning, Frank had stayed overnight in hostels, but lately life has finally improved.
"He moved into a new apartment and met a girl," Luis told radio station KGO.
Luis Galicia argues she doesn't know who's want to hurt his younger brother.
He was a good man with a wide heart.
"He always pampered his family by preparing a tasty meal and cooking lunch," said Luis Galicia
He never worried to get involved in quarrels.
He was the brother who adapted to the others.
"Given everything that has gone wrong in the world, he was like a raw diamond that shone brightly every day", he says.
Anyone who has information about what has happened is urged to call SFPD Information number 415-575-44444.
