Do smile confess?
This step embarrassed Moscow.
Sergejs Ivanovs is an ancient and close ally of Vladimir Putin and, just like Putin, once worked in the Soviet security service in the KGB.
In this position, he was one of the most influential men in Russia.
At a public televised meeting, the two men said Ivanov rejoicing on his own initiative.
But in spite of camera-focused smiles, rarely confess such an explanatory, especially before the parliamentary elections.
Is this an outcome related to the struggle for power?
Nobody doesn't know.
