Primark buyers are shocked by a woman brazzily in the middle of a lingerie store.
Buyers felt uncomfortable when a woman began unmasked to try panties in the middle of the store.
Further aggravating the situation, she ordered them to make sure that they suit her and then took off, putting panties back on the store's shelf.
She kept searching for clothes at Folkeston Bouverie's shopping mall shop and made four more panties.
Primark store Bouverie Place in the shopping center in Folkeston – the place where this woman made the undercoat and then put it back on the shelf.
At that time, there was a mother of two children, Jenny Davidsson, who tells that an unfamiliar woman put on her clothes and left the store without buying anything.
She points out that people couldn't believe their eyes.
Walking in the middle of the store, she took underpants from the shelf, pulled off her tights and trousers and surveyed them on the spot.
She didn't even try to find a more discreet place to measure them, she just tended them on site.
Everyone watched how she took off the panties and, apparently, the woman didn't like them, because she just put them back on the shelf.
She surveyed three more panties until she decided that she didn't like any of them and left the store.
It didn't look like she would be worried that someone was watching or thinking about a person who would buy the clothes she tried on.
Mrs Davidson (33 years) from Kent, says: "The idea that someone will buy clothes that have been tried on by another person and which have not been washed afterwards."
Incident took place Tuesday afternoon.
Mrs. Davidson adds: "I suppose the store's staff picked these clothes out of the store's shelves after her departure - which is also acceptable."
I couldn't imagine being able to buy a new undercoat and find out that another woman has ordered them and then they haven't been washed.
Primark's spokesman said Primark was aware of the incident that took place on Tuesday, August 9.
Specific clothes have been removed from store shelves.
How to protect yourself from firefighters using Krav Maga
The world is a dangerous place, but this video from Dailymail.com could make it a little safer.
To find out how to protect yourself in the near distance from attackers with a firearm, we talked to Krav Mag's grandmaster from New York Rone Mizraki.
Regardless of whether you are attacked from the front or back, this video shows you how to protect yourself and prevail over an attacker.
Mistress points out, if an assaper is attacked from the back, it is necessary to rotate first in order to clearly see the attacker and avoid the trajectory of a shot.
Then the weapon should be grasped between your front arm and the shoulder and make a beating in the opponent's face with your free elbow.
Then there's a punch with a knee in the groin and while the attacker strays hurts, he's having to take up his weapon, hit him in the face with a breeze and retreat, continuing to draw the weapon against him.
If the attacker is approaching from the front, the situation is similar - the trajectory of a shot should be avoided, you need to grasp the weapon and tremble it in such a way that the villain can't scrotnate.
At the same time, pressure should be exerted on the weapon and make a beating to the opponent on his chest and finally take away his weapon and retreat continuing to aim at him.
It sounds complicated?
Watch the video to see exactly how Mizraki is doing.
But you remember, if you'ren't Krav Mag's master, then it's safer to give your money to the robbers.
