Akropolis LT, which operates Akropolis sales and entertainment centers in Vilnius, Klaipėda and Šiauli, will be merged with Akropolis Group group, inheriting all current obligations to Akropolis LT partners and employees.
Akropolis LT and Akropolis Group are expected to be merged until 1 October this year.
We are launching a new development phase, during which we will carry out large-scale projects, so we are trying to simplify the company's structure - this will allow Acropolis to create a more effective team of professionals within LT and Akropolis Group.
At the moment, we are carrying out the largest Acropolis development projects within a decade - the construction of the multi-purpose shopping center Akropole in Riga and the development of a multi-purpose object in Vilnius, in the former Velga Plant territory.
"The structure of the new company will make it possible to more effectively use the experience and competencies of Akkropolis LT team by successfully developing projects and operatively making the necessary decisions", admits Saule Zabulionytė (Saulė Zabulionytė), Akropolis Group board member.
"Akropolis Group" is a group of companies that manage real estate development, shopping center rental and management companies in Lithuania, Latvia, Estonia and Bulgaria.
