600 000 salmon cubs will be admitted to the Daugava.
This week, during Latvenergo, salmon and sea trout woven muneraries are being introduced this week in the Daugava near Mangaļsala, and this year it is planned to release more than 600 000 one-year-athlet and sea trout cubs grown in the fish farms of the scientific institute Bior Tome and Dole.
Latvenergo LETA was informed that the introduction of fish will continue for the next few months - every year 6, 300 000 cubs and larvae of different species are introduced into the water bodies of the Daugava basin.
In the spring and beginning of the summer 2016, pike and lamprey larvae will be skipped, in June it will be possible to snatch snails, in July - snapper and vimbas in August and September.
Māris Kuņickis, Director of Latvenergo’s production, told that caring for the environment is one of the cornerstones of Latvenergo Group’s sustainable development.
"Everwhile is aimed at environmentally-friendly actions in close co-operation with the scientific institute Bior, carrying out the cultivation and election of fish fry in the Daugava basin, as well as realizing other activities," Kuņickis pointed out.
More than 600 000 one-year-aternal loaves and sea trout pups will be admitted to the estuary of the Daugava River this year.
For the second year in a row, fish fry is marked before being released, cutting off the fatty fin.
There are 25 000 salmon babies with an average weight of 31.3 blelves today.
Every year in a scientifically substantiated composition of the species and in a numerical amount in the river Daugava and in the water bodies of its basin there is an introduction of juvenile comrades and larvae.
In accordance with the laws and and regulations, the propagation of fish resources shall be carried out in the Daugava and water bodies of its basin, on the basis of the expert-certification of the losses caused to Latvenergo as a result of the economic activity of Latvenergo and providing a conclusion on what compensatory measures are to be carried out in order to ensure the diversity of fish resources.
The State Environmental Service, on the basis of the abovementioned expert-examination, takes a decision on the amount and type of compensation.
Latvenergo's annual compremuneration in the fish resource recovery program is 1 035 000 euros.
In the spring of 2016, Latvenergo in cooperation with the association "We for Fish" for the fifth year deploys 400 artificial spawn nests in the Daugava near Kaibala and Ikšķile.
Collaboration with the association by promoting natural spawning of fish is Latvenergo an additionally supported initiative within the framework of the Fish Reservation Programme.
Placing artificial spawning sockets in the reservoir is an important event that contributes to the protection and propagation of fish resources in the Daugava.
