Reid argues if Clinton will be elected president, she will appoint Garland as Chief Justice.
Harry Reid, the leader of the Democratic Party of the Senate, is convinced that if she becomes president, then she will nominate Merrick Garland as Chief Judge of the Supreme Court.
The Senate Republican Party has blocked Garland's endorsement since March, when he was nominated by President Obama.
