A spokeswowoman for a raid later said that he hadn't personally talked about this topic with Clinton and these were just speculations.
He commended Garland and said Clinton's team wouldn't "stowing a boat" with another choice.
Garhlands is the chief judge of the U.S. Columbia District Appeals Court.
Reid said the Republicans blocking Garland's nominee are "inclinations" and behaves in the interest of Republican Party presidential nominee Donald Trump.
He also said that Trump wasn't suitable for president.
