Rajevsky estimated that both Kučinskis and Reizniece-Ozola in this government the approval of the SRS leader is the "first big decision", which can affect their future as politicians.
If it is now starting to change the stance in the choice of a candidate for the position of the head of the SRS, then it will negatively affect their image in the public administration.
The working agenda of next week's meeting of the Cabinet of Ministers includes the issue regarding the relocation of VVD Head Kolegova in the position of the Director-General of the SRS, according to the government's working order.
Koļegova was promoted to the position of the Head of the SRS by the Minister of Finance Reizniece-Ozola after Ināra Pētersone re-registered from the service management and when the competition for the position of the Director-general of the SRS ended without a result.
Dace Pelēkā, Acting Head of the SRS on Thursday, August 11, conceded in an Interview with Latvian Radio - if she was offered a candidate for the position of a manager, then she could agree.
The Minister of Finance, however, later admitted that he does not yet consider other candidates for the position of the Head of the SRS.
Raivis Dzintars, the leader of the parliamentary faction of the National Alliance, also admitted that the NA still supports Koļegovs under the leadership of the SRS.
In Spain, the chances of reducing the budget deficit are threatened by incapacitated to form a government.
A month a month ago, the European Commission (EC) issued an opinion that Spain and Portugal did not take sufficient measures to reduce the level of the deficit to 3% of gross domestic product (NGP) requested by the euro area.
Estimates that, in spite of austerity, the Portuguese budget deficit at the end of last year was 4.4% of GDP at the end of the last year and 5.1% in Spain.
However, the European Commission decided not to impose economic sanctions on both countries, at the same commensurate, while setting fiscal targets for the near future.
One of the reasons why the EC, however, did not impose sanctions against these two countries is the increasing Euroscepticism in many countries of the European Union.
Additional sanctions would only increase such negative sentiments.
Critics, however, argue that the EC does not be conservative in its decisions, from the outset agreeing on unified rules and then failing to apply them in life.
For example, the President of the German Bundesbank Jens Veidmann has pointed out that Europe loses its credibility in this way, creating an idea for the citizens that the rules of the European Union are suggestive rather than binding.
The EC has now proposed and all the Member States have approved an extension of the deadline for raising the deficit until the end of this year for Portugal and for Spain until 2018.
During the coming months, the European Commission promises to examine the progress achieved by the two countries, at the same time pointing out that both Spain and Portugal should be prepared to introduce additional austerity measures, if circumstances so require.
Preliminary projections indicate that Portugal's target could be achieved in due time and already this year the budget deficit could fall to 2.5% of its gross domestic product.
This means that, as part of the Stability Programme, the government of this country must implement austerity measures worth 0.25% of GDP this year.
These measures should be included in this year's budget, with an additional focus on controlling the cost of purchasing goods and services.
In the case of Spain, the situation is much more complicated.
The budget deficit should be reduced to 4.6% this year, to 3.1% next year and 2.2% of GDP in 2018.
In addition, in the next two years, consolidation measures should amount to 0.5% of GDP each year.
It is particularly difficult to achieve these objectives that for eight months Spanish political parties have not managed to agree on the formation of a government, and there is an increasing possibility for Spain to hold pre-valid parliamentary elections for the third time in a year.
Concern opinion polls, however, would not significantly change the political scene of the third elections in the country as well.
The most popular party continues to be a nation party led by current Prime Minister Mariano Rajoy, which would once again win less than 33% of the vote in the election.
Only the Socialists have attracted their popularity a little, while the popularity of "Podemos", or "Together We Can" and "Ciudadanos" or "Citizens", have declined a little.
The People's Party wants socialists and "Ciudadanos" involvement in the government still this month, otherwise it will not be possible to adopt and submit a draft budget for 2017 to the European Commission until mid-Octo-Octo-Octo-Octo-Of October.
Rafael Hernando, a spokesman for the People's Party parliamentary faction, as stated by the People's Party's parliamentary faction if the government succeeds and the parliamentary elections will still be held for the third time, Spain will become a European commeasurance.
The cleanliness of the beaches in the Gulf of Riga is critical.
During the fifth year surveying beaches, activists have concluded that, unfortunately, the number of rubbourcies found is increasing every year, and most bathing visitors are to blame here.
The most pollulied bathing places are in Riga.
The capital city council explains that bathing areas every day are tidy, but it is quite difficult to fight against dirty visitors.
In addition, waste left on the dry state during rainfall can be washed into the water, thus greatly damaging its quality.
Excluding Liepaja beach and separate places in Courland, the cleanliness of the beaches elsewhere in Latvia is critical.
Volunteers of "My Sea" have circulated such a communication this week.
For the fifth of the fifth years, the road along the throe along the Gulf of Riga has concluded that the number of rubbage left by the population has increased every hundred meters.
Sadly, a critical assessment has come up this year.
"We can see that this will be the year when the number of garbage on the beach of 100 meters can probably even exceed 200 units," says Jānis Ulme, a spokeswoman for the expedition "My Sea".
According to Latvian Radio, he was located on Tūja beach, where the procession of volunteers along the Gulf of Riga continues.
Earlier this year, among the various household rubbish and remnants, activists had to collect even day-light light bulbs that have been left to weed in the sea sand.
Ulme, a participant and organizer of the hike, the population is to be blamed for the pollution.
"The main source is the visitors of the beach themselves, because more than half of the total number of garbage is plastic, a variety of garbage, starting with bags, plastic pieces that are already at the declining stage, it is no longer possible to identify them, and butts, bottles, corks", says Ulme.
Among the dirtiest beaches there are also bathing places in Riga.
For example, in Daugavgrīva every one hundred meters, on average, almost 800 units of waste have been collected, which is critically a lot.
Campaign organizers also explain that there are also signs of warnings or prohibitions placed everywhere at every step.
"Multiple figures for all three bathing places in Riga - Daugavgrīva, Vakarbuļļi and Vecaki - unfortunately come together large and far beyond the desired goal, to which Latvia is supposedly moving, to reduce the number of waste units to 135 units by 2020", concludes the environmental defender.
Cleaning of bathing places in Riga takes place every day, on the hottest days of the summer even twice, explains Uģis Vidauskis.
However, the fight against dirty visitors is quite difficult.
We are returning to the cultural issue of these people.
"Those who litruise, use alcohol, smoke and do all those things that can't, don't even take special signs," Vidauskis points out.
That's why Vidauski asks bathing site visitors to report polluters to the police as well.
Can be called the police, boldly point out these violations and in this way everyone to fight.
Perhaps some new warnings can be imposed, but, as I said, it will hardly change the situation as radically.
"Since everyone should simply turn together and be intolerant of such transgressors", he emphasizes.
In the meantime, water quality measurements have been carried out this summer for the fourth time by the Health Inspectorate, which can impose a ban on official bathing sites.
This year, just like for other years, the quality of the water is good and satisfying everywhere.
At the moment, the situation is such that in all 56 bathing areas the quality of the water has been good all the time and there are no bathing restrictions.
"For the last time we will take the analyses at the end of August", says Normunds Kadiķis, Senior Environmental Health Specialist of the Inspectorate.
During heavy rainfall, the rubbish on the land can be washed into the water.
This, in turn, can affect its quality, the environmental specialist points out.
Rotations in the elite of Russia are continuing - a change of leader in Putin's administration.
Thawing the position himself?
Vladimir Putin has informed the Russian media that Sergei Ivanov wished to quit this position himself and from now on he would be the president's special representative for nature conservation, ecology and transport.
Announcing the changes, Putin in front of the television cameras paid tribute to Ivanov: "Dignified Sergey Borisovich, we have been working together with you for many years and are doing it successfully."
I'm happy with how you perform the responsibilities assigned to you.
I am well reluctant about our agreement not to use you for more than four years.
That's why I'm comprehenscribe your desire to change the field of activity.
And I hope that also in the new position you will make full use of your knowledge and experience.
However, it is emphasized that the leadership of the presidential administration is a very significant position and it made Ivanov one of the most influential people in the country.
In view of the fact that the elections of the State Duma are expected in Russia next month, there are rumours that this step is related to the fight for power in the Russian political elite.
Ivanov has also been called a possible replacement for Putin as president, so the allegiance that he himself wanted to occupy the office of a president in matters of nature conservation and transport has raised doubts.
According to Lsm.lv archive, Ivavnov is a Colonel-in-Chief of the KGB and the Federal Security Service.
Ivanov has been an ancient and close ally of Russian President Vladimir Putin.
He started his career in the special services in 1975, where he got acquainted with Putin.
Later, when Putin became the head of the Federal Security Service, Ivanov became his deputy.
In turn, at the end of the relucency of the first Russian President Boris Yeltsin was appointed Secretary of the Russian Security Council.
In 2000 after Putin came to power, Ivanov's "Information Security Doctrine" was approved, which, among other things, predicted resuscitating state censorship mechanisms in Russia.
Sergejs Ivanov became the Minister of Defence of Russia in 2001, but already in 2005 he was the deputy Prime Minister Mikhail Fradkov and was responsible for the development and arms exports of Russian defence companies.
Now, after leaving the office of the head of the presidential administration, Ivanov will also retain a seat in the Russian National Security Council, where the new head of the president's administration Vaino will also work.
Guilt comes from the family council party in the elite.
Ivanovs himself recommended the position of the Head of the Presid’s Advisance to Vaino.
Anton Eduardovich has long been acquaintance with Anton Eduardovich.
Also from the time when we worked in the government under your leadership.
And in the last almost five years we have been communicating practically every day.
"Therefore, I'm sure that by all professional and personal character traits he's ready for this job," Ivanov said.
Guilt comes from a family that belonged to the Soviet party's elite.
His grandfather Carl held high positions in the Estonian Communist Party, including its first secretary for a decade until 1988.
"Medouza" with a reference to the book "Estonian Self-determination and Independence" writes that in the late 80's Karl Vaino allegedly asked Moscow to give permission to use force against the demonstrators.
However, he had received a refusal and soon lost his position.
Shortly after, Guino has moved to Moscow.
Anthony Vaino has graduated the Moscow Institute of International Relations and is fluent in Japanese.
However, he's gone from the diplomatic service to work in the president's protocol's administration.
It has already been announcing that in the last mischievous Russia has been shocked by the dissemination of several high-ranking officers and even arrests, including the replacement of governors and federal representatives of several constituencies.
According to politologists, President Vladimir Putin reorganizes the prevailing elite ahead of an upcoming elections in 2018.
One of the main traits - more and more often representatives of power structures are at the leading positions.
