"Porgy un Besa" is a story about love, its volatility, passion, as well as household tragedies and simple everyday joys.
It reflects African-American vitality, music and rhythm.
Precisely this lack of political correctness in this opera, this exclusion of tolerance makes it so agitative.
"And yes, this love story is extraordinarily powerful, exceptionally beautiful and in some way really profound," says director Viesturs Kairišs.
What I like the most - by listening or sounding this opera, there are always such punctuations - famous melodies, famous motifs, but these transitions from one character to another, illuminating one character or the other character, or choir, or or orchestra.
"It's the most thrilling, this building," the opera is judged by Andris Poga, the conductor and conductor Andris Poga of the concert stage of the opera "Porgijs un Bessa".
The visitors of the opera unanimize that this is a grandiose event.
It's a great pleasure for them to hear this world-famous Guerswin's opera.
Blissful that in Liepaja you can feel the breath of the world.
"Execution professional", the opera is judged by visitor Edgars Lāms.
The concert stage was special due to the fact that the orchestra played in the newly opened concert hall "Great Amber" for the first time in the orchestra bleer and for the first time a concert performance of the opera took place.
The square next to the renovated building of the Art Museum could be named Janis Rozentāls.
The Deputy Mayor of Riga Andris Ameriks said at the opening of the anniversary exhibition of Rozentāls that the museum's own address in the future could not be Krišjāņa Valdemāra iela 10a, but Jaņa Rozentāla laukums 1.
Māra Lāce, director of the museum, admitted that re-registering the address will create a good bureaucratic burden, but in general, this idea is appreciated and, therefore, agreed with the suggestion of the local government.
The city of Riga put a kind of foundation stone for this idea in 1936, creating Burkardis Dzenis’ monument to Janis Rozentāls, which stands next to the museum.
Vilhelms Purvītis was one of the initiators for the creation of this monument.
In this way, this distant action could be purely logical.
I've been gnawed a little of my constigence all the time - but Vilhelms Purvītis, where we're going to put his name?!
"But if you, Mr Amerika, promise to think"... said Lāce.
It has been reported that the National Museum of Art building officially opened its doors in May this year after extensive reconstruction and modernization.
Reconstruction of VEF Culture Palace will finally begin this week.
“Velve” will be re-established for approximately 11 million euros.
It is planned to renovate several premises of the castle, including two spectator halls, as well as adapt the building to people with reduced mobility.
The Riga City Council has planned to attract six million euro money from European Union funds for the project, but Oļegs Burovs, the Director of the Property Department of the Riga City Council, admits that for the time being there is no complete clarity for the project about European funds yet.
"Despite the fact that the political will to embrecommote VEF's Culture Palace's repairs by attracting the European structural funds is, we are waiting for a decision for months, real action from officials of the Ministry of Finance, there will be that money allocated or not", says Burovs.
In December of last year, we were told that everything depends on Brussels.
Two weeks ago, the Ministry of Finance received a letter from the European Commission that you will decide itself that Brussels would not take a decision here.
At the moment, we are seeing the formation of another circle of discussions, well, then let's see what we can expect in the next few days.
"I would like to say that the Riga City Council undoubtedly guarantees that this process will have been started and completed within deadlines," Burovs points out.
It has already been reported that more than a year ago in March 2015, VEF Culture Palace collectively hosted a farewell concert ahead of an immediate renovation.
Although a year has elapsed, the renovation of the building had still not been commenced and collectively continued to work unsuitable.
Renovation of VEF Culture Palace has been divided into seemingly independent reconstruction works, where everyone will ensure the implementation of different functions of the palace.
The first - increasing the accessibility of the VEF Culture Palace and the improvement of the surrounding area.
It envisages arranging the surroundings and utilities, as well as to restore the facade of the building.
The second - improvement of VEF Culture Palace service offer.
It envisages the restoration of the interior, walls and ceilings of the building, stage and sound recording studio, as well as to arrange internal engineering communications of the building.
The third - the improvement of the working conditions of creative amateur collectives, which includes plans to improve workshop equipment, room heating and ventilation systems.
Before the 40th anniversary of "Līvu", you can get acquainted with the legendary rock band at an exhibition in Liepaja.
The exhibition presents a variety of "Līvus" characteristic objects - photographs arranged in a timeline to reflect the activities of the group from origins to 2010, when it announces the end of the group's activities.
There will also be exhibited stage costumes, musical instruments, awards and concert recordings, as well as other things unseen to the general public, which reflected the creative activity of the band "Līvi".
The exhibition will be complemented by objects of the collection of the Liepāja Museum.
The visual design of the exhibition was created in cooperation with fashion artist and painter Elita Patmalniece.
Musicians, who have been associated with the band "Līvi" and their loved ones, also withdrew a vocation and shared both objects and memories.
"Līvu" dates back to 1972, when a vocal instrumental ensemble was created at the Liepāja Culture House, led by Juris Pavītols.
The ensemble took part in the festival "Liepaja dzintars" in 1972 and 1974, as well as in city and republishers.
A fateful meeting took place in 1976, when Juris Pavītols met Ēriks Ķiģelis and the Metalurgs Culture Palace founded a group, inviting Ingrīda Gūtmane, Andris Krūziņš and Jānis Grodums to join.
Over the course of the years, the composition of the group has changed more than once.
Participants have joined, others went their own way, some have returned.
However, most importantly - the desire to confess that Latvian rock music is able to live and exist - has remained the same.
"What wasn't shrinking - ginsothes, hairy and bearded, these boys seemingly differed from the generally accepted stereotype of stage singing," the music reviewer Klass Vāvere says about the band.
In addition to the musicians mentioned above, there were such outstanding musicians as Igo, Vilnis Krieviņš, Modris Šterns, Valdis Štarks, Laimis Rācenājs, Tālis Pusbarnieks, Ainars Virga, Aivars Brīze, Guntars Mucenieks, Dainis Virga, Toomas Kleins and many others.
Entrance to the exhibition is free of charge.
The exhibition can be viewed from August 19 to October 30.
On August 27 in Liepaja concert garden "Pūt, vējiņi" will take place group "Līvi" 40-year anniversary celebration "LĪVIfest 2".
For the first time in the 8-in-a-month period, there has been inflation in Bulgaria.
In July, Bulgaria's national statistics showed 1% monthly inflation.
This is the highest rate since 2012 and the first indicator above zero since the previous year was positive (0.2%).
The average annual inflicted on the CPI in the last 12 months (August August-July 2016), compared to the previous year, was -0.8%.
Compared to the previous year in July 2016, the consumer price index was 101.9% compared to the previous year and the average monthly inflation was 1.0%.
From the beginning of the year, the inflation rate was -0.2% (in July 2016 compared to December 2015) and annual inflation in July 2016 was -0.2% compared to July 2015.
Compared to the previous month, in July 2016 there was an increase in prices for the following groups of consumer goods: meals and non-alcoholic beverages (1.7%); transport (1.8%); entertainment and cultural events (6.3%); hotels and restaurants (1.2%); household goods and services (0.3%).
Prices of garments and shoes decreased (2.2%); for home appliances, household appliances and regular home cleaning (0.5%); health (0.1%).
Prices remained at the level of the previous month for alcohol and tobacco, management, water, electricity, gas and other fuels, communications and education in the previous month.
