Then it speaks to the people.
But in Cesis, in the Lamp discussion, you said that "must be returned to an understanding of a full man".
What do you mean?
Does this mean that a person turns away from the message of the church?
And does the church have such a repentance today?
A dying man dying on the road in the Indian capital is roaring.
In the Indian capital, no one has seemed to know about a dignified man dignering on the road - it turns out that he landed an hour on the side of the road and then still robbed, the BBC informs the BBC.
It has been reported that a man who had been identified as a Matibulon drove a rickshaw during the day but worked as a security guard at night.
Matibulon at 5:30 a.m. in the morning went home along the road when he was knocked down by a passenger car.
A recording of follow-up cameras shows that the driver got out of the car to look at the victim and then drove away.
After an hour, when no one has seemed to know about the bleeding man, he was robbed by a garnished.
Approximately 90 minutes after he was knitting, police arrived at the scene and the victim has been taken to a hospital where he died of injuries.
Revoking her candidacy for the position of Director-General of the State Revenue Service (SRS), Inga Koļegova, the Head of the State Environmental Service, rebuked the government out of the fall, believes Ojārs Skudra, an associate professor at the Faculty of Social Sciences of the University of the University of Latvia.
Koļegova's explanation for withdrawing the candidacy in relation to controversy in the ruling coalition is related to the dissoposal that she has prevented the fall of the government.
Skudra in a conversation with agency LETA expressed that it is difficult for him to concede that "Unity" would support Kolegova's candidacy next week at a government meeting "Unity".
Consequently, if "Uniterity" ministries voted against, but Kolegova would still be confirmed in office, it would lead to the resignation of the government.
Koļegova also consults both the Minister of Finance Dana Reizniece-Ozola and Prime Minister Māris Kučinskis prior to the announcement about the withdrawal of the candidacy.
At the Same time, it is a concede to "Unitedness", which strongly opposed her candidacy.
Predictioning whether it will be possible to find a suitable candidate with the help of the competition, Skudra admitted that there are two options - either a compromise figure will be selected, or the institution as acting director-general will continue to lead Dace Grey.
At the same time, however, he points out - if the Minister of Finance has so far stated that another candidacy has not been considered, it is a hug to Grey that he should not take part in the competition.
LETA has already announced that Kolegova, the Head of the State Environmental Service, has decided to withdraw her candidacy for the position of the Director General of the SRS.
Due to "Unity" objections, the government postponed Koļegova's confirmation as Director-General of the SRS for a week for a week.
According to the government's decision, Kolegova testified that she is still ready to become the head of the SRS.
However, later her thoughts changed - on Friday, in an application to the Minister of Finance Dana Reizniece-Ozola, she points out that she is withdrawing her consent to relocating the position of the head of the SRS and this is not an easy choice for her.
Andrejs Vaivars, press secretary of the Prime Minister Māris Kučinskis, explained to LETA that a new competition will be organized for the vacant position of the Director General of the SRS.
In the center of Riga there was a crash involving a police car.
A road traffic accident occurred in the center of Riga this afternoon, involving a State Police car.
A police car with an audible and light signals switched hurried to the highest-categorical call until Krišjānis Barona and Dzirnavu streets collided with a different car at the intersection of Krišjāņa Barona and Dzirnavu streets.
Police are explaining the circumstances of what had happened, but the initial information indicates that the other vehicle had not missed a police car.
A woman was injured in the accident.
Population has shrunk in Riga this year
At the beginning of this year there were 638 784 inhabitants in Riga, which is 0.34% less than in 2015, when 641 000 inhabitants were officially registered in the capital, the Central Statistical Bureau (CSB) told LETA.
However, in terms of population, the capital of Latvia ranks 30th among the capital cities of the European Union (EU) countries and large cities with a population of more than one million.
According to the EU statistical office "Eurostat", Riga has the highest proportion of women - the capital of Latvia is convincificing in the first place among Europe's largest cities with 127 women per 100 men.
In all the three capitals of the Baltic States, there is the largest proportion of women in Europe's largest cities: in Vilnis they are 123, and in Tallinn 121 women per 100 men.
