A reconstructed road section has been uncovered in Medumi.
Uldis Augulis, SJSC Latvijas Valsts ceļi (LVC), as well as representatives of builders SIA "Binders" and local governments today unveiled the reconstructed section of the Russian border (Grebņeva)-Rēzekne-Daugavpils-Lithuanian border (Medumi) (A13).
The roads are a business card of the state, especially border roads, so it is a particular pleasure to discover a reconstructed link on the border with our southern neighbours.
This is another example of the fact that, thanks to co-financing from the co-financing of European Union funds, the situation on the country's main roads is improving.
"According to forecasts, during this planning period, the funds available for roads will be acquired already in 2018, and we need to think about how to continue to maintain the most loaded motorways in a very good quality, as well as to ensure the mobility of the population in all regions of Latvia without the financing of the European Union," Uldis Augulis emphasized when reconqueling the Symbolic Ribbon.
The Minister of Transport also pointed out that proposals prepared by traffic experts on sustainable financing for Latvian roads will be presented to the government in the near future time.
Construction works from Medumi to the Lithuanian border (156.4-163.05. km) SIA Binders was started last year and this year it was continued after a technological break.
Reconstruction costs are €13.5 million (inclest VAT), co-financed by the European Regional Development Fund (ERDF). The project was co-financed by the European Regional Development Fund (ERDF).
"In the reconstructed section of the road there has been a complete renovation of the road structure and next year the repair works will be commenced in the next section from Medumi to Daugavpils itself, so the entire road from the Lithuanian border to Daugavpils will be arranged," informed Jānis Lange, Chairman of the Board of the LVC.
The country's main highways are most loaded, and by 2018, we plan to get all the country's main roads in good condition.
The next task will be to maintain them in a good quality, providing periodic maintenance in a timely manner and carrying out the replacement of an asphalt surface every 7-9 years.
"That, of course, will require adequate funding, and all travellers are looking forward to the proposals developed by an expert group for the arrangement of the road financing system," Lange noted.
Within the framework of the project, road connections and lighting in Medumi center have been arranged.
Significant ground works have been carried out: in the four-strength of large-scale decay and embankment works have been carried out, the long-circuited road profile, which until now was very uneven.
Public transport stops have also also been restored and a rebuild turnaround area for public transport has been built.
Previously, the road had insufficient load-bearing capacity and the terrain terrain was not transparent due to mountainous valleys, as well as an old road common terrain.
In the next construction season it is planned to rebuild the section of the motorway from the border of the city of Daugavpils to the now reconstructed section (144,80-156,40 km).
This this year LVC plans to carry out different types of works in more than 1100 kilometres of public roads.
Information about all repair works planned in the national road network this year is available on the LVC website www.lvceli.lv.
"In order to achieve the desired weight-loss results, the right choice of food combinations is very important", admits Lithuanian nutritionist Laura Romeraite-Kuklieriene.
In addition, it is easy to do in the summer period, when fresh fruits, berries and vegetables grow in our own gardens.
Thought-thought combination of dietary products can help not only to reduce excess weight, but also to purposefully promote a variety of processes in the body.
Macaroni and odish is a successful combination, because it provides a long-lasting feeling of satiety and helping to fight fat.
Studies published in the European Journal of Clinical Nutrition have shown that vinegar has a beneficial effect on the level of glucose in the blood and helping us to feel vigilant.
Cayenne pepper and protein-flavour-rich, such as poultry meat or a protein cocktail, create not only a feeling of satiety, but also reduces the cravings for large meals for the next meals.
Such a combination of dishes is also able to increase the calorie amount burned after a meal by up to 35%.
Studies have shown that Caising pepper can help to get rid of fat in the belly area.
Eggs contain a metabolic-bodied nutrit - choline, while paprika is a good source of vitamin C.
Quantify levels of cortisol can also be reduced when consuming a sufficient amount of this nutrit, hence the accumulation of fat around the middle part of the body.
Oatmeal porridge, to which fresh charcoons are added, is another delicious and fat-burning meal for breakfast, which it is worth to include in your menu.
Oatmeal flakes and embankments contain fiber, which, according to the conclusions of Canadian scientists, controls ghrelline - anticontriguing hormone - and, therefore, a sense of hunger.
In addition, berries contain polyphenols, which are helpers in reducing weight, as well as do not allow the formation of fat.
Vegetables and proteins are also able to draw miracles in reducing weight.
Such a combination is able to create a feeling of satiety.
Vegetables contain water and fiber, so promote the feeling of satiety.
At the same time, the protein slows down the digestive process and provides a feeling of satiety for a longer period of time.
At lunch, you can eat a chicken with a salad or make a protein cocktail from the finished mixture and enjoy it together with your favorite vegetables.
What combinations of products should be avoided.
The fruits contain sugars - monosaccharides or disaccharides - compounds of one or two molecules.
By contrast, the starch, which is found in the vegetables, is a polysaccharide.
Fruits decompose in the stomach mechanically, while chemically they do not decompose until they reach the third or fourth degree in the process of digestion, which occurs in the gut.
Starch decompletes in three different stages, which begin already in the mouth.
Therefore, it is important not to eat sweet food immediately after a meal.
Eating sweet food immediately after a meal, it is "trapped" in the stomach along with other dishes, where it is not chemically digested and begins to blew.
Don't eat bread, potatoes, peas, bananas, dates or other carbohydrate-containing products with lemons, lime, oranges, grapefruits, pineapples or other sour fruits.
Enzyme ptyalin contained in saliva acts only in an alkaline environment.
Fetal acids inhibit not only the digestion of carbohydrates, but also contribute to their fermentation.
Don't eat eggs and meat, nuts and meat, cheese and eggs or cheese and nuts, meat and milk, eggs, milk or nut or nuts and similar combinations of protein-rich products per meal.
Their processing requires a variety of indigestion, each of them with different strengths, features and a time to enter the stomach.
Aquarium, honeymone, muskamelone and other melons should always be eaten separately from other dishes.
Melons do not be digested if they are in the stomach along with other foods.
Fat in combination with protein-fledged products.
Fats form a successful combination with starch, however, the same can not be said about fats and proteins - fat inhibits the digestion of proteins.
Substances can be combined with a very small amount of fat.
If a large amount of protein-containing products is consumed, avoid fat use altogether.
This also applies to rawness - it is not recommended to combine a large amount of nuts (contains protein) with a healthy avocado (contains fats).
Such a combination inhibits effective weight reduction.
How better to cook?
"Coconusing, heat treatment leads to a significant loss of nutrients - about 15% to 55% of the original nutrient composition of the products," the nutritionist points out.
In in most cases, the nutrients are lost by boiling foods in the water.
However, the nutritional value of certain foods increases by directly boiling.
It is recommended to use the remaining liquid after cooking vegetables - in this case, you will not lose the nutrients left in the water, and you will be able to eat them later.
It is also recommended to prepare vegetables by steaming them.
Heat treatment significantly increases the bioavailability of lycopene contained in tomatoes.
Boiling tomatoes for a period of 30 minutes, the lycodine volume increases by 25%.
Heat treatment also significantly increases the bioavailability of betacarotene, which can be found in red-yellow, orange plants such as tomatoes, carrots, sweet potatoes and spinach.
Heat treatment of eggs and meat deprives the natural properties of the protein contained in them, making it more easily digestible.
Heat treatment of meat and eggs also makes the iron and other minerals contained in these products more easily absorbed by the body.
It should also be borne in mind the fact that the freezing of products can reduce the amount of vitamin C from 10% by up to 90%, but the freezing of fiber does not affect.
Beans in combination with tomatoes can increase iron intake in the body, which, in turn, ensures better functioning of the brain and muscles.
Our body ingests up to 33% less non-blood-causing iron found in plant products such as beans, deciduous foliage, cereal-based products other than cloven-causing iron found in animal products such as beef, fish and chicken.
You can significantly increase non-bloustrative iron absorption in the body by consuming non-blood-providing iron-containing products together with sources of vitamin C, such as oranges, tomatoes and berry.
Vitamin C helps to change non-bloody iron in such a way that our body absorbs it more easily.
Iron is necessary for the production of hemoglobin, which ensures the delivery of oxygen to the muscles and the brain.
In order to get the most out of the lettuce, add to them healthy fat, such as olive or linseed oil.
When brewing sandwiches with salmon, add with vitamin D to rich salmon or sardines unspecified yogurt, which is a good source of calcium.
Vitamin D increases the amount of calcium in the gut and plays an important role in the formation of bones.
Oats (as well as other wholemeal products), along with vitamin C sources such as strawberries, blackcurrants, raspberries and other fruits or berry, help stabilize cholesterol, as well as to avoid obstruction of arteries.
Snapchat "Anime" effect criticizes assassuination
Snapchat representatives say this filter is inspired by animation, but some commenters claim it is racially insensible.
With this lens effect, Snapchat allows 150 Millions of Users to Change Reality and Play with Their Identity in a Samnorary Everyday Life.
You can turn yourself into an pineapple, a dog or an image that fits into a painting by Roja Lihštenstein.
Lenses are foggy, immudying instruments that generate more than 30 million re-modated selfies per day.
Any bug quickly becomes publicly noticeable.
The effects of Snapchat lentils have been criticized in the past, receiving reproaches that the application popularises overly-anguted or light skin tones of the face as a benchmark of perfect beauty.
This week, the new effects of lenses were published, which allows users to form crouches for eyes, crouches and round cheeks, and some critics dubbed it a racisstic Asian cartoon – “yellow face”.
It was also asked whether such contradictions do not indicate that the company has greater problems with diversity.
News and public negations flared up on Wednesday, when editions The Vergge and "Motherboard," told reporters that lens effects had been removed from the app.
The company explained that the goal of the lens is to portray Anime's characters, rather than caricature people of Asian descent.
But people who have experienced racism, these effects were reminiscent of painful stereotypes.
Others categorically denigrated similarity with Anime.
A Korean-born American feature-study student Greisa Sparapani's Twitter post about the images gained a widespread resonance. In an e-mail, she points out that the effects of the lens are "offifying and embarrassing, to not say more."
She added that it is difficult not to overlook the apparent similarity between Asian caricatures and lens effects.
This suggests that the effect of the lens is not simply a yellow face, but a yellow face in the sense of racism.
Snapchat isn't the only company that has fallen into these cultural traps.
American culture is also involved in an unfortunate struggle for diversity and inclination, ranging from company meeting rooms to Hollywood and devices we use on a day-to-day basis.
And Snapchat's large audience of young people, representing a variety of races, unlike older residents, is more sensitive to such things.
If Snapchat lenses create an image that insults the users, then "these things don't go unnoticed nowadays, 25-year-old Katie Žou said in an interview on Thursday.
On Thursday, Medium Product Manager Žou eradicated his Snapchat app and advised others to do the same.
In her article “Medium,” and telephony, she explained that, in her opinion, problems related to the race arise due to Snapchat's employment policy, which insufficiently supports the diversity of dewies.
Žou criticized the company's management, which consists mainly of white men and then concluded his article with a reference #DeleteSnapchat.
"This means that there is no racial divergence in the company, so such decisions are tolerated. Do some representatives of other races work in the company, but they don't occupy such a position to be able to reluctantly and comfortably express their opinion," believes Chinese-American Zhou.
Others also agree with her opinion, while Snapchat hasn't responded to her complaint.
The company doesn't reveal how many employees are represented by different races, pointing out that it's a private company.
Snapchat declined to discuss the origins of its employees, but its spokeswoman revealed that the company has hired a staff specialist who will focus on ensuring that racial minorities are also represented in the company, which are not widely represented and will contribute to their integration into the company.
Žou, on the other hand, won't rebuild his Snapchat account, adding: "It's interesting if they really need more users like us to realise it isn't right."
The House of Congress announces that military officials misrepresented reports of the Islamic State.
In a statement released on Thursday, the confectionary chamber states that representatives of the U.S. Central Order misrepresented reports, portraying the war against the Islamic State in Iraq and in Syria much more optimistic than it is in reality.
Analysts of the Central Command's proprietary express general dissatisfaction at the interim report of the task unit set up by Armed Forces Committee, the Intelligence Committee and the Republican Representatives of the Defense Financing Sub-Committee, pointing out that their leadership controlled reports of American success in the fight against the Islamic State.
The central command, known as Centcom, is a military base in Tampa, Florida, which overtosee U.S. military operations in the Middle East and Central Asia.
Relative news about this report says that intelligence reports, confirmed by high-ranking Centcom executives, reflect the U.S. fight against terror more positively than they are in reality. Facts were regularly misrepresenting better achievements rather than other intelligence analyses.
Renal spokeswoman Ken Calvert of California says: "Centcom action is unacceptable - our soldiers are the ones suffering when our policy makers receive false messages."
Centcom's management mistakes can be found in the organization's supreme leadership.
This 10-letter-long report illustrates in detail the existing problems of the Central Command's reflection and analysis of the efforts of the Americans to prepare Iraqi forces in 2014 and 2015.
Although it doesn't provide irrefutable evidence that senior officials of the Obama administration would have misrepresented the reports, this suggests that Centcom's management has exerted some pressure on the analysts to portray a more optimistic view of the threat posed by the Islamic State (also known as ISIS or ISIL).
According to the report, in the first half of 2015, press releases, announcements and reports of the Central Authority to the Congress portrayed the situation in a significantly more positive light than it was in reality.
For example, representatives of Centcom publicly stated that Mosul's regativating surgery could begin as early as April or May 2015.
Mosul is Iraq's second-largest city, which is still under the control of the Islamic State.
Make Pompeo, a spokesman for Kansas Republican Party, said in a report: "Multi-Month-century investigation clearly confirms this."
From mid-2014 to mid-2015, U.S U.S. Central Governance officials misrepresented reports, portraying ISIS jiyties in Iraq's weaker ones than they were in reality.
The Republican Party formed a working group, finding out that the analysts are frivolous that information about the Islamic State is being misrepresented.
As the Investigation continues, a report published on Thursday will be accompanied by new discoveries in the case.
