São Paulo Governor Geraldo Alckmin's proposal foresees the closure of almost 100 public schools, while 300 000 students will be relocated to other schools with a view to saving money.
Some demonstrators drew graffiti with messages against interim President Michael Temer.
This protest took place only a few days after the previous protest, when students gathered in demonstrations with the aim of expressing support for the dismissed president Dilma Rousebef, whose impeachment was voted for by the senate.
