"Latvenergo" follows the process of opening the gas market also from the position of a potential trader.
Latvenergo, the state energy company follows the process of launching the gas market from the position of both the consumer and a potential trader, said Ivita Bidere, a spokeswoman for the company.
"Decision on whether "Latvenergo" gas market will also be joined as a trader in the future, will be determined by what gas market model and the regulatory framework will be established."
"Therefore, for our part, we are actively involved in the creation of regulatory enactments and commenting, as well as submit our proposals," Bidere said.
Agency BNS already wrote that the Ministry of Economics (EM) in cooperation with the Public Utilities Regulatory Commission and the energy company "Latvijas Gāze" has developed the Cabinet of Ministers Regulations Project "Regulations Regarding Trade and Use of Natural Gas", which will change the existing natural gas market operating principles, providing natural gas users with the right to freely choose a natural gas trader as of April 3, 2017.
When working on the new regulation of the natural gas market, EM aims to make the natural gas trade process as easy as possible and comprehensible.
Therefore, as the most effective and most convenient service solution for the user, a "hydraulic model of the trader", in which all activities related to customer service are provided by the trader - one contract, one invoice and one place for the provision of information and customer service, leaving the technical issues of the natural gas-distributing system to the operator of the distribution system.
A similar solution is currently being implemented in electricity trading.
We would like to remind that a gradual opening of the market is planned for household users - even after 3 April 2017, those household users who do not wish to choose another natural gas trader will be able to continue to receive natural gas from the existing trader at a regulated price, thus becoming related users.
"In such a case, the obligation to supply natural gas to related users at a regulated price is imposed on the public trader," the ministry informed.
Merchants, in turn, will have to choose a natural gas trader with which a natural gas trade contract must be entered into.
Until entering into a natural gas trade contract for a certain period of time, trade of natural gas will be ensured by the current natural gas trader at a specified price.
The draft regulations of the Cabinet of Ministers stipulate in detail the rights and responsibilities of a natural gas trader, system operator and users.
This Regulation prescribes the procedures by which natural gas shall be supplied to users and the supply thereof, the requirements for the safe use of the natural gas system, the requirements for the safe-to-use of the natural gas system, the public trader, the system operator, the user of the system operator, the user and the gasified object; the procedures by which settlements shall be settled for the services received shall be performed, the amount of late payment per cent, the procedures for changing traders and the supply of customers in the event of natural gas supply; the procedures in which the supply of natural gas shall be ensured by a public trader.
