Minister: next week it is planned to look forward to increasing the remuneration of the SRS Director-General.
Finance Minister Dana Reizniece-Ozola (Union of Greens and Farmers (ZZS) next week plans to talk with Prime Minister Māris Kučinskis (ZZZS) and government coalition partners about increasing the remuneration of the Director-General of the State Revenue Service (SRS).
Reizniece-Ozola told reporters on Friday that the issue of increasing the remuneration of the Director-General of the SRS needs to be solved urgently in order to make this position more attractive to potential candidates for the re-competition.
There will also be talks next week about changing the conditions of the competition.
The Minister also emphasized that she doesn't think any particular candidate to address the vacant position.
Reizniece-Ozola at the same time expressed the opinion that Inga Kolegova, the Head of the State Environmental Service Inga Koļegova, would have been a good Director-General of the SRS.
With regard to Dace Pelēko, the current SRS Acting Head of the SRS, who has expressed her readiness to apply for this position, reiterated the opinion that the new Director-General of the SRS should have an "look from the outside" and should not come from the structure of the SRS.
She also emphasized that she was looking forward to returning the Saeima to advance the amendments to laws necessary for the re-organization of the SRS as soon as possible.
Agency BNS has already announced that Inga Koļegova, the Head of the State Environmental Service, Dana Reizniece-Ozola (ZZS), has submitted an application, in which her candidacy for the position of Director-General of the SRS has been revoked.
In the submission, she expressed that it is not an easy choice, but over the last two weeks, her loved ones have undergone serious emotional pressure, although they have not carried out any acts reprehenscribed by law.
Kolegova also pointed out that discussing her candidacy has heightened controversy among the ruling coalition parties, which is also unacceptable.
It has also been reported that Ināra Pētersone, the former Director General of the SRS, left the post at the end of June.
Naphtha prices continue to rise; stock indices in the U.S. and Europe are rising, as well as U.S. dollar value.
Oil prices in the world continue to rise on Friday morning, investor sentiment is positively influenced by the statements made by the Saudi Minister for Oil, which intensifies anticipation that major oil-winners will take action to stabilize the world's oil market at an upcoming OPEC meeting in September.
The three main U.S. stock exchange indexes on Thursday reached a record-scalf that hadn't been seen since 1999.
