Kurdu activists occupy the building of the German public broadcaster.
A 30-strong Kurdish group on Thursday evening captured the public broadcaster WDR's building in Düsseldorf, where nearly a two-hour prosecution was held, German police reported.
Demonstrators, who arrived with posters taken, chanted various slogans, trying to pay attention to the current situation in Turkey.
According to the officials, the demonstration has generally taken place peacefully, and the protesters, at the request of the staff, have eventually voluntarily left the building.
Insurer pays compuls compensation to passengers on a cancelled flight at the airport on Wednesday.
If Apdrošināšana has disbursed a travel insurance indemnity to a family for a flight cancelled at Riga Airport on Wednesday, August 10, due to which it was necessary to relinquish the visit to the planned music festival.
On August 11, an indemnity application was received from a customer in Insurance.
The family had planned to go to a music festival in Belgium, but since it was not possible due to the flights canceled at the airport on Wednesday, it was calculated to the customer for the reservation, which could no longer be revoked, as well as the festival tickets purchased in the amount of 204 euros.
On the other hand, the airline has promised to be recompensated to customers for the money spent on the plane's tickets.
If Insurance from all indemnities of travel insurance on an average of 15% of cases has paid compensation for the interruption or cancellation of a trip.
"At such times, expenses are remunerated for the purchase, return or exchange of tickets, as well as for the reservation of the accommodation," says Dagnija Rutka, Head of The Insurance Persons Risk Insurance Product.
As it is known, on the evening of August 10, a private airplane ceased due to technical problems on the runway of Riga Airport, so only several departing flights were cancelled, but several incoming flights had to be relocated to other airports.
Due to the repair of the neighbor, the man gets a crushed ceiling and forced to quit the house.
Dmitrijs Saidyaševs, whose neighbor has beaten the overhaul in his apartment, and since then Dmitry has been dressed from the ceiling and there is no certainty that it is unsuccessful to stay in the apartment.
The problem is that my neighbours carried out arbitrary construction and there is a damaged ceiling in my apartment.
Then I informed the Riga Construction Board, a house manager and other organizations.
The construction board said we'ren't an operative service and we don't have any expert.
"The owner of the apartment has to go to the Latvian Association of Engineers, and from there there will be an expert," Dmitrijs says.
The invited expert has arrived, recorded what had happened and admitted that the coverage was in an unsatisfactory condition.
However, a month has elapsed since Dmitry's application to the construction board, and until the beginning of this week no one was able to answer whether being in the apartment is not life-threatening.
The construction board said - that's the legislation, wait, if you're not satisfied, write to everyone in a row.
"Then I wrote to the Riga City Council, but they forwarded the house to the governor, then the manager of the houses again to the construction board, and then there is an impasse", says Dmitrijs.
After reviewing the whole pile of papers, it is clear that the construction works have been stopped, although from time to time it can be heard that someone is working there.
Within a further period of two months, an expert-examination has to be carried out and within six months the apartment owner, who performs the repair works, must be rectified.
An independent expert has drawn up its opinion, but the building authority considers it incomplete and superficial.
The expert did not indicate whether the metal grid in this load-bearing structure has been touched, so there is no certainty that there is a danger to the owner of the lower apartment.
"Therefore, we have requested an additional explanation from this expert," says Ilze Žūka, a spokeswoman for the Riga City Construction Board.
Regardless of the prohibition to carry out any repairs in the upper apartment, it is still accustomed from there that the construction is continuing.
Punishment for arbitrary construction without a building permit is from 70 to 700 euros, but in this particular case the penalty can be much more severe.
As long as an expert's opinion is awaited, the building authority has taken a decision that the two apartments may not be exploited - both in which the construction works are taking place and Dmitry apartment.
"This is an unprecedented case in the practice of the building authority, when in this way due to their ignorance or simply reluctance, residents may have posed a threat not only in their own property, but also to the owner of the lower property, as a result of which this owner cannot exploit his or her property," says a spokeswoman for the construction board.
Now it remains for Dmitry to look for another place to live - with relatives, friends, in a hotel or to rent another apartment.
But Dmitrijs can try to recover from a neighbor in a civil law, which can take a lot of time.
Due to arbitrary construction, it is currently forbidden to stay in both apartments until the construction engineer will give his/her conclusion, and it may have to wait even for three weeks.
Losses incurred will have to be borne by the owner of the apartment where repairs have taken place.
The owner of this apartment has not been taken into account due to what has been taken into account by the building authority is also threatened with imprisonment for a period of up to six months.
