Reconstruction of the former Ķemeri sanatorium into a five-star hotel will cost 22 million euros.
Creating the former Ķemeri sanatorium into a five-star hotel "Park Hotel Ķemeri" will cost 22 million euros, Gita Želve, a spokeswoman for the future hotel manager SIA "Park Hotel Ķemeri", tells LETA.
Creation of a hotel is the first reforestation of the Kemeri former sanatorium.
The second stage will be "wellness" or wellness clinic, which is planned to be unveiled in 2022, while the opening of the hotel is expected in May 2018.
Želve points out that the exact cost of the clinic is not yet known at the moment.
However, she points out that it will be located in the former building of the resort polyclinic with an area of about 12 000 square meters.
The clinic will be deployed on three floors.
"Park Hotel Ķemeri" and the owner of the contemplated clinic is an international fund "G Capital Europe", which invests in European assets.
The owners of "G Capital Europe" are a number of investors who invest money in this fund, Želve points out.
George Jones, CEO of "G Capital Europe" previously, plans to invest €12 to €15 million in the creation of a former resort polyclinic, totalling €30 to €30 million.
It has already been announced that in the renovation of the cultural-historical park with an area of more than 42 hectares, the restoration of access roads and street sections, the construction of an interactive nature tourism object, the improvement of the territory and the construction of parking lots on Emīla Dārziņa Street, which will promote the socio-economic development of the city of Jurmala and an increase in the number of tourists, the Jūrmala City Council plans to attract 14.5 million euros from European Union funds, co-operating with three to four million euros.
By the middle of 2017, design works are planned, but the construction works and arranging works will start in the autumn of next year.
As reported, it is planned to create a five-star hotel "Park Hotel Ķemeri" and "wellsness" in the historical sanatorium complex "Ķemeri".
However, the reconstruction protracted.
In turn, it was stated in the annual report for 2010 that "Ominasis" regularly communicates with the hotel operator "Kempinski", which continues to ensure day-to-day technical control in the sanatorium "Ķemeri", and already in 2011 it will definitely be "construction of the future hotel "Ķemeri" and immediately the preparatory works for the opening of the "Kempinski" chain hotel will begin.
In October 2014, "Park Hotel Ķemeri" confirmed its readiness to purchase the total belongings belongings belongings belongings belonging to the insolvent "Ominasis Latvia", but a month later the auction was recognized as having not taken place, because the winner did not pay for the purchase in due time.
The selling price was determined according to the starting price of the last unsuccessful auction - EUR 2.86 million.
