The President will present the Order of the Three Stars to the opera singer Antoņenko.
The President of Latvia Raimonds Vējonis next week, on August 16, will present the Order of the Order of the Order of the Three Breeds to Alexander Antoņenko, according to the President’s agenda.
Ceremonial Ceremony will take place in the House of Blackheads at 13 p.m.
According to the information provided by the Latvian National Opera and Ballet (LNOB), Antoņenko gradivated the Jāzeps Mediņš College of Music in 1998, where he studied wind instruments and studied sing at Margarita Gruzdeva.
He has Studied at Jāzeps Vītols Latvian Academy of Music Vocational Department Arvīds Lustes.
Graduated at the Latvian National Opera Choir in 1997, but in 1998 he made his debut with Oberto's Role in G.F.Hendell's opera "Alčīna".
Having received the "Great Music Award 2003" for the vocal performance in opera performances and Verdi Requiem.
It is pointed out that in the 2004/05 season he became the most internationally acquaintance Latvian tenor, where the world's largest opera houses.
Since the autumn of 2004, he has been singing "Düsseldorf Deutsche Oper am Rhein, Berlin and Grace, Dresden's "Semperoper", Oslo and Stockholm's Royal Opera, London's Covent-Garden Opera, Monte Carlo Opera, the Vienna State Opera, as well as the Geneva, Dresden and Düsseldorf.
Antoņenko debuted with great success in the Metropolitan Opera Prince's role "Nāra".
In 2011, Antoņenko sang the title role in Othello's Paris Opera with Rikardo Muti and the Chicago Symphony Orchestra, at Covent-garden's opera, he sang Luiji in the new production of "The Settlement", as well as participated in Christopher Loya's "Girl from the West" staged in Stockholm.
A year later Antoņenko sang Otello's role with great success at London's Covent-Garden Opera.
